Z||000000||magnum||04-05-2001||07:18 PM||||I think I'm gong to go with a built 3.1. Talked to a guy from Whitehorse who builds  them.(ever heard of them?). Said I would have about 240-250 HP. What kind of power is that 0-60 and also compared to a stock Mustang or Camero. ||||reg||1
Z||000001||rogergarrison||04-05-2001||07:20 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by magnum:<BR><B>I think I'm gong to go with a built 3.1. Talked to a guy from Whitehorse who builds  them.(ever heard of them?). Said I would have about 240-250 HP. What kind of power is that 0-60 and also compared to a stock Mustang or Camero. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I get 270 with turbo from my 3.1 iron head<P><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=9116379&p=34556781"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||WKDFIRO||04-05-2001||11:42 PM||||250 hp from a 3.1?<P>Would that be with a turbo? Is that with the stock block? Stock pistons?<P>The most we could squeeze out boring, stroking, milling the heads, upgraded valve train, upgraded exhaust, bigger injectors, evening shortening the deck to raise compression we could barely break 200 hp estimated.<P>Your mechanic may be a little enthusiastic about a 3.1. The 3.4 would probably be a safer bet if you want those kind of numbers!<P>Though if there is a 3.1 normally aspirated motor out there putting out those kind of numbers I would sure like to know what voodoo they did and see the dyno specs! ||||reg||5
Z||000003||magnum||04-06-2001||03:00 AM||||It's an HO engine bored out to 30 over. Plus has a few high performance parts. Please tell me it this sounds too unbelievable so I don't waste my time and money. I must admit I don't know allot about engines, that's why I'm here asking everyone's opinion. Thanks ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Fiero-Tex||04-06-2001||10:09 AM||||I think that someone is not telling you the truth about the horsepower, or maybe it's not a 3.1.  I have a fiero with a 3.1 stroker kit. Roller rocker arms, computer chip, ect. , and I am not getting 240-250 Hp.  I am getting something more like ~190Hp maybe less.  I have not had this dyno tested, but I think I would notice a 100Hp difference from the stock engine.  Good Luck!<BR>||||reg||13
Z||000005||WKDFIRO||04-06-2001||06:28 PM||||All Fiero 2.8 V6 were HO right from the factory. They had larger valves than the 2.8 found in the Firebird/Camaro set ups. The heads from the 3.4 Firebird/Camaros used the same valve heads and had more reenforced blocks. <P>I would seriously look at what the 3.4 would cost you in your area before rebuilding a 2.8. It might be easier and in some cases cheaper to get a prepared 3.4 long block and then have the mechanic install it. I say this not because I would have anything to gain but because I wish I had done it after I blueprinted and upgraded my 2.8! Plenty of pick up but since I did it before it was well known about the 3.4 I always get to wonder what it would feel like to do all the things I did to the 2.8 to the 3.4. Until Im proven wrong, I will NOT believe that the 2.8 block will see over 200 hp without forced induction and/or nitrous.<P>If I ever found a big sack of money I would have my Fiero in Chris West's shop waiting for 3800 SC myself...but thats just me.||||reg||14
Z||000006||DoD||04-06-2001||10:39 PM||||Maybe this discussion could be cross-referenced to "Max. horsepower with OEM computer", elsewhere on this site?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Will||04-07-2001||11:07 AM||||240-250 HP is quite possible. 300 Hp is possible. The amount of power you get is more limited by the streetability you desire. I think 240-250 HP out of that engine is on the edge and maybe a little beyond what is good for street driving.<BR>Whitehorse does kit cars, don't they?||||reg||1
Z||000008||WKDFIRO||04-07-2001||01:51 PM||||Anything, they say, is possible...<P>How is it possible then, Will, for a 2.8 to attain 300 hp without forced induction or nitrous? Is the engine life measured in weeks? Are we talking about a 2.8 beyond using pump gas as a fuel source? I was under the impression that we were still talking about the stock iron block and not the all aluminum Bowtie block. <P>What have you done, Will, and most importantly, where are the dyno specs to prove it!||||reg||6
